# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large data and generated artefacts.
#
# The working tree is ~18 GB, almost none of which belongs in version control.
# Sizes measured, not guessed:
#
#   dfc2019_data  16 GB   licensed benchmark dataset (IEEE DataPort)
#   venv         1.5 GB   virtualenv, rebuildable from requirements
#   final_out    316 MB   generated meshes and textures
#   scenes       100 MB   saved scene snapshots
#   cache         81 MB   cached depth fields
#   india         13 MB   downloaded imagery crops
#
# GitHub rejects files over 100 MB outright and warns above 50 MB, and the
# individual GLBs here are 26-49 MB each. None of it is source, and all of it is
# reproducible from the code plus the documented data sources.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Benchmark dataset -- licensed, and far too large to redistribute.
# Obtain from IEEE DataPort: 2019 IEEE GRSS Data Fusion Contest, Track 3.
dfc2019_data/

# Python environment
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_# checkpoints/ stays out. The only checkpoint here is the smoke-test model:
# 1 epoch on 2 tiles on CPU, which scored MAE 7.16 m against the pretrained
# baseline's 6.68 m and a correlation of -0.121. train_height.py's own guard
# says not to swap it in. It is 372 MB in one file, over GitHub's 100 MB
# limit, so it would need Git LFS -- most of a free account's quota spent on
# a model that is worse than doing nothing. Re-add once a real run beats the
# baseline.
checkpoints/

# Generated 3D output: meshes, textures, DSMs, baked maps
final_out/
viewer/output/
cache/
india/
*.glb
*.obj
*.mtl
*.ply

# Generated rasters. The pipeline writes many of these; none are inputs.
*.npy
segmentation_preview.png
segmentation_raw.png
relative_depth_preview.png
ortho_*.png
overlay_cleaned.png

# Run logs and scratch files from interactive sessions
*.log
scratch_*.py
scratch_*.png
prev.py
chk*.py
diag_*.py
tune_seg.py
test_overlay.py
find_block.py
find_india.py
probe_extent.py
screen_tiles.py
colab_subset.zip

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# More generated output and dataset copies found when first staging.
# colab_subset/ alone was 483 MB of licensed DFC imagery -- a copy of the
# dataset, not source, and not redistributable.
colab_subset/
dfc_out/
demo_out/
verify_out/
taj_out/
out/
colab/depthwizard_modules.zip

# Imagery. Blanket *.png / *.jpg was used at first and is too blunt: it silently
# blocks screenshots for the README and any UI asset the viewer might need, and
# a rule that quietly drops files someone deliberately added is worse than one
# that lets a stray raster through -- the stray gets caught by review, the
# missing file does not.
#
# So imagery is ignored where it is GENERATED, and allowed where it is authored.
*.tif
*.tiff
final_out/**/*.png
viewer/output/**/*.png
india/**/*.jpg
india/**/*.png

# Ad-hoc renders land in the repo root during interactive sessions
# (ortho_*.png, taj_wide.png, s_zoom.png, visual_noshadow.png ...). Ignoring
# images AT THE ROOT ONLY keeps those out while leaving authored assets in
# subdirectories committable. The leading slash is what scopes it to the root.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Explicitly allow authored assets.
!docs/**
!README*.png

# Tauri build output. The Rust target directory reaches several GB, and the
# installers are build products rather than source.
src-tauri/target/
dist/
*.msi
/*-setup.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added with the GAMUS work and the dashboard.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GAMUS subsets. The full dataset is 80 GB and CC-BY-4.0 licensed by its
# authors; what is here is a downloaded slice, reproducible with
# `python gamus.py download`, so it is not source.

# Fine-tuned model weights. Hundreds of MB per checkpoint, and GitHub rejects
# any file over 100 MB outright. The training report JSON is the part worth
# keeping, and it is small -- but it lives alongside the weights, so the whole
# directory goes and the report is quoted in BENCHMARK.md instead.
checkpoints/

# Images people upload through the dashboard. Not ours to redistribute.

# Stage timings are calibrated per machine. Committing this laptop's numbers
# would give a different machine wrong ETAs on its first run, which is worse
# than having none -- progress.py already handles an empty calibration.

# One-off experiment scripts, same convention as the diag_/tune_/chk_ rules
# above. Each answered one question and is superseded by the measurement it
# produced, which is recorded in BENCHMARK.md.
ab_metrics.py
ceiling_test.py
compare_fp.py
mvs_test.py
profile_build.py
sweep2.py
sweep_recall.py
test_ground*.py
test_ortho_poly.py
test_sc_real.py
test_vdvi.py
tune_minh.py
tune_mvs_seg.py

# Tauri generated sources (icons, platform scaffolding) are build products.
src-tauri/gen/
